jQuery Mobile Practical Viva Questions with Answers
1. What is jQuery Mobile?
jQuery Mobile is a touch-optimized web framework used to create responsive mobile websites and web applications using HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

2. What is responsive web design?
Responsive web design means a website automatically adjusts its layout according to different screen sizes like mobile, tablet and desktop.

3. What is the purpose of jQuery?
jQuery is a JavaScript library used to simplify DOM manipulation, animations, event handling and AJAX operations.

4. What is the difference between jQuery and jQuery Mobile?
jQuery	jQuery Mobile
JavaScript library	Mobile UI framework
Handles DOM and events	Creates mobile interfaces
Used for scripting	Used for responsive mobile websites
5. What is data-role in jQuery Mobile?
data-role is a special attribute used to define jQuery Mobile UI components like page, header, footer, button and listview.

Example:

<div data-role="page">
6. What is data-role="page"?
It defines a mobile page container in jQuery Mobile.

7. What is data-role="header"?
It creates the top navigation/header section of the mobile page.

8. What is data-role="footer"?
It creates the bottom footer section of the mobile page.

9. What is data-role="listview"?
It creates a mobile-optimized styled list used for menus and navigation.

10. What is data-theme?
data-theme applies predefined jQuery Mobile color themes.

Example:

data-theme="b"
11. What is the use of viewport meta tag?
It makes the website responsive on mobile devices.

Example:

<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
12. Why do we use CDN links?
CDN links are used to load external libraries like jQuery and jQuery Mobile from online servers.

13. What is a CDN?
CDN stands for Content Delivery Network.
It delivers files quickly from distributed servers.

14. Why is jQuery Mobile called touch optimized?
Because it is specially designed for touch devices like smartphones and tablets.

15. What is the purpose of CSS in this practical?
CSS is used for styling the webpage such as colors, spacing, gradients, fonts and layout.

16. What is border-radius in CSS?
It is used to create rounded corners.

Example:

border-radius:10px;
17. What is box-shadow?
It adds shadow effects around elements.

Example:

box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
18. What is a gradient in CSS?
A gradient is a smooth transition between multiple colors.

Example:

background:linear-gradient(to bottom,#dfe9f3,#ffffff);
19. What is hover effect?
Hover effect changes the appearance of an element when mouse pointer moves over it.

Example:

transform:scale(1.02);
20. What is the use of forms in the website?
Forms are used to collect user input like name, email and feedback.

21. What is <input type="email">?
It is an input field specifically designed for email addresses with basic validation.

22. What is <textarea>?
It is used for multiline text input.

23. What is the purpose of navigation links?
Navigation links help users move between different pages of the website.

24. How does navigation work in jQuery Mobile?
Navigation works using page IDs.

Example:

<a href="#about">
It opens:

<div id="about">
without reloading the page.

25. Why is jQuery Mobile good for mobile websites?
Because it provides:

responsive UI

touch support

lightweight design

easy navigation

cross-platform compatibility

26. What is mobile-first design?
Mobile-first design means designing the website primarily for mobile devices before desktop devices.

27. What are the advantages of jQuery Mobile?
Easy to use

Responsive design

Touch optimized

Cross-platform support

Fast development

Lightweight framework

28. What are the disadvantages of jQuery Mobile?
Limited advanced UI customization

Slower than native mobile apps

Less modern compared to newer frameworks

29. What is HTML?
HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.
It is used to create webpage structure.

30. What is CSS?
CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.
It is used for webpage styling and layout.

31. What is JavaScript?
JavaScript is a scripting language used to make webpages interactive.

32. What is a framework?
A framework is a collection of pre-written code used to simplify development.

33. What is the purpose of <head> tag?
It contains metadata, title, CSS links and script files.

34. What is the purpose of <body> tag?
It contains all visible webpage content.

35. Why did we use multiple pages in one HTML file?
jQuery Mobile supports multiple pages inside one HTML file using:

<div data-role="page">
36. What is the purpose of ui-content class?
It provides proper spacing and mobile-friendly layout.

37. What is the purpose of ui-btn class?
It converts normal buttons into mobile styled buttons.

38. What is the purpose of ui-btn-b?
It applies theme B styling to buttons.

39. What is the purpose of listview inset?
data-inset="true" creates rounded and padded list appearance.

40. What is the output of this practical?
A responsive multi-page mobile website for I2IT Academic Portal created using jQuery Mobile.
